of Tennyson's *Princess* (*Home they brought her warrior dead*, &c.), are typical examples. Wordsworth's *Daffodils*, Shelley's *Skylark*, Keats's *Grecian Urn*, Milton's *Penseroso*, Burns's *Field Mouse*, Herrick's *Rosebuds*, Lovelace's *Lucasta*, Shakspere's *It was a lover*, may serve to illustrate; but attempts to distinguish lyric poetry clearly from other kinds (epic, dramatic, elegiac, didactic, &c.) have not been successful, the classes not being mutually exclusive.
>>>

